This code should not be merged until the Meadow.Core team has some bandwidth.
The Meadow.Core team needs to:
 - Decide the time format to be used in notifying Meadow.Core about an interrupt.
 - Update `Meadow.Core` to accept notifications with the new time format added.
    This commit adds a 64-bit field containing the Nuttx tick count at the time the
    interrupt occurred.

Since the message size has increased, `Meadow.Core` will also need to be modified
to match. This will require both `Meadow.Core` and `Meadow.OS` to be updated on
the Meadow platform at the same time. Or additional code will need to be created
for both `Meadow.Core` and `Meadow.OS` that allows older `Meadow.Core` to be used
with `Meadow.OS` with this commit's code.

Peter Moody
02Oct2025
